+
+Host-rule tests of the Cake four-stream mHC training package (no GPU needed).
+
+The registry ``cake_jit.py`` carries the integer host rules of the kernels
+(``k1_units``, ``k7_chunks``, ``k6_grid``, ``k2_grid``, the one-trip row grids
+``k3_grid`` / ``k4_grid`` / ``k5_grid``, the design's persistent ``row_grid``,
+the token padding and the workspace regions) as plain Python.  The same rules exist in
+the kernels' own test harness; :data:`RULES_ROWS` is that harness's table of
+record -- one row per (token count, SM count) over the 28 token counts the
+contract names (the 16 correctness values and the 13 performance rows) and
+the SM counts of the three target products -- and the registry must reproduce
+every row bitwise.  The module also checks the registry's literal tables (the
